\fs32\b The Header Form\b0\fs20\par
\par
The Header Form contains the information which identifies the batch being transcribed and the people associated with it.\par
\par
It is normally completed when starting a new transcription. If any of this information needs to be changed later, use Edit Header to display the Header Form again.\par
\par
\fs24\b Batch details\b0\fs20\par
\b Record type\b0  - Select Births, Marriages or Deaths according to the index being transcribed.\par
\par
\b Year\b0  - The year of the index.\par
\par
\b Quarter\b0  - The quarter of the year being transcribed. This is required for indexes before 1984.\par
\par
\b Page source\b0  - Identifies the source from which the page being transcribed was obtained.\par
\par
\b Page\b0  - The page number of the index being transcribed.\par
\par
\b Suffix\b0  - Any suffix associated with the page number.\par
\par
\b Page letter\b0  - Any letter associated with the page.\par
\par
\b Volume format\b0  - Specifies the format used for volume numbers in this index.\par
\par
\b Source reference\b0  - An optional reference identifying the source scan. When supplied, this can help WinBMD2 locate the correct scan automatically.\par
\par
\b Comments\b0  - Any general comments associated with the transcription batch.\par
\par
\b Credit name\b0  - The name to be used for the transcription credit.\par
\par
\b Credit email\b0  - The email address associated with the credit.\par
\par
\b Credit type\b0  - Specifies the type of credit to be used.\par
\par
\fs24\b Contributor details\b0\fs20\par
\b Original creator\b0  - The FreeBMD User ID of the person who originally created the transcription.\par
\par
\b Creator email\b0  - The email address of the original creator.\par
\par
\b Syndicate\b0  - The FreeBMD syndicate associated with the transcription.\par
\par
\b Current FreeBMD User ID\b0  - Your FreeBMD User ID. This identifies the person currently working on and uploading the transcription.\par
\par
\b Password\b0  - The password associated with the current FreeBMD User ID and used when uploading to FreeBMD.\par
\par
\fs24\b Starting the batch\b0\fs20\par
When the required information has been entered, click Start batch to begin transcribing.\par
\par
If you want to continue work on a transcription which already exists, use Open existing batch instead.\par
